# Third-party data sources

Canonical registry: **`.cursor/third-party-sources.yaml`**

## Agent behavior

- Before scraping or calling external Star Citizen / trade / starmap APIs, **read the registry**.
- If an `accepted` (or solid `trial`) source already matches the purpose, **use it** — do not ask the user which website to use.
- When you find a new useful source and successfully use it, **add an entry** to the YAML (`status: trial`, then `accepted` after a good fixture pull). Fill `id`, `purpose`, `url`, `used_by`, `notes`, `added`.
- **Do not delete** registry entries unless the user asks. Humans remove or mark `rejected` when a source is bad.
- Keep `used_by` paths accurate when adding scripts or fixtures.

## Status values

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `accepted` | Prefer this source for its `purpose` |
| `trial` | Newly added; OK to use, promote after proven |
| `rejected` | Do not use (leave for history, or human deletes) |
